# Draft Recommendation Logic

- Keep recommendation scoring deterministic and explainable. Changes should preserve visible notes, suggestion labels, and insight text when scores shift.
- Filter unavailable players using both draft picks and already rostered players before ranking candidates.
- Respect league roster settings when deciding draftable positions. Do not show K, DEF, IDP, or other positions unless the league settings make them draftable.
- Preserve draft board modes: active rookie drafts should use rookie-only boards, while dynasty season views can keep the full player pool.
- Prefer shared domain helpers for primary position, flex eligibility, draft-aware rosters, pick ordering, and Sleeper search-rank sorting.
- Add focused tests for scoring, filtering, board mode, and roster-slot behavior when changing recommendation logic.
